{"episodes":{"173028":"A persistent surge of warm, moist, and unstable air led to a broken line of strong to severe thunderstorms moving southeast across southern WI. Numerous reports of large hail were received along with wind damage in the Beloit area.","173549":"A decaying line of thunderstorms exited Wisconsin and provided a glancing blow to Michigan and Indiana. There was least one instance of tree damage in northern Indiana and one instance of sub severe hail in Michigan. In the vicinity of this line of storms, wind was strong with gusts near 50mph.","173550":"A decaying line of thunderstorms exited Wisconsin and provided a glancing blow to Michigan and Indiana. There was least one instance of tree damage in northern Indiana and sub severe hail in Michigan. In the vicinity of this line of storms, wind was strong with gusts near 50mph.","173827":"Scattered thunderstorms moved across portions of northern Illinois during the afternoon and early evening of September 20th.","173828":"Scattered thunderstorms moved across portions of southern Lake Michigan on September 20th.","173973":"A cool and wet pattern will persist through mid-week as an upper level low remains stalled off the central California coast. An anomalously deep low pressure system yield periods of light to moderate precipitation with a few isolated thunderstorms through Wednesday before the low ejects 19-20 Sept before ejecting northeast 21-22 Sept into the northern Rockies.","174039":"A cool and wet pattern will persist through mid-week as an upper level low remains stalled off the central California coast. An anomalously deep low pressure system yield periods of light to moderate precipitation with a few isolated thunderstorms through Wednesday before the low ejects 19-20 Sept before ejecting northeast 21-22 Sept into the northern Rockies.","174082":"An isolated severe thunderstorm brought large hail and damaging wind gusts.","174287":"A weak mid level trough over South Florida led to the developme